    "descriptionChirho": "A precious gem formed within a mollusk shell, used in the NT both literally (as valuable merchandise, Rev 17:4, 18:12,16) and figuratively (the pearl of great price, Matt 13:45-46; pearls before swine, Matt 7:6; gates of pearl, Rev 21:21). The two clusters split on grammatical number: S71927 collects plural forms (pearls, with-pearls) and S71928 collects singular and mixed forms (pearl). All translations confirm a single lexeme: eng 'pearl/pearls,' spa 'perla/perlas,' hin moti/motiyom (मोती/मोतियों), arb lu'lu' (لُؤْلُؤ), kor jinju (진주/진주들), swa 'lulu' invariant across number.",
